{"term":"virtue","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:83f62e682f8f4406d7","definition":"The idea of all that is good or excellent (in every sense of those terms) in a human being, collectively instantiated by a varying number of human traits known as \"the virtues\", the enumeration of which vary by the many virtue systems which have developed within different cultures, religions, and historical periods.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["douth","thew","goodness"],"antonyms":["vice","foible"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["by virtue of","in virtue of","cardinal virtue","dormitive virtue","in virtue of which","lady of light virtue","make a virtue of necessity","nonvirtue","patience is a virtue","pseudovirtue","unvirtue","virtuecrat","virtued","virtue ethicist","virtue ethics","virtue is its own reward","virtueless","virtue name","virtue signal","virtue signaler","virtue signaling","virtue-signaling","virtue signaller","virtue signalling","virtue-signalling","virtuous","woman of easy virtue"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/virtue#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c845a8f94acb733ef8","definition":"Accordance with moral principles; conformity of behaviour or thought with the strictures of morality; good moral conduct.","example":"Without virtue, there is no freedom.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["douth","thew","goodness"],"antonyms":["vice","foible"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["by virtue of","in virtue of","cardinal virtue","dormitive virtue","in virtue of which","lady of light virtue","make a virtue of necessity","nonvirtue","patience is a virtue","pseudovirtue","unvirtue","virtuecrat","virtued","virtue ethicist","virtue ethics","virtue is its own reward","virtueless","virtue name","virtue signal","virtue signaler","virtue signaling","virtue-signaling","virtue signaller","virtue signa